Third-party code and text included
----------------------------------
- aa_evals/scicode/vendor/scicode/ and aa_evals/scicode/templates/  SciCode helpers and prompt templates
  (https://github.com/scicode-bench/SciCode). Apache License 2.0; full text in aa_evals/scicode/vendor/LICENSE.
- tb_agents/deepseek_v41_encoding.py  adapted from the DeepSeek V4.1 reference encoder as shipped in vLLM
  (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm). Apache License 2.0; copyright the vLLM project contributors (SPDX header).
- aa_evals/hle/prompts.py  answer and judge prompts of Humanity's Last Exam
  (https://github.com/centerforaisafety/hle). MIT License.
- aa_evals/omniscience/prompts.py  answer and grader templates from the AA-Omniscience public dataset card
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/ArtificialAnalysis/AA-Omniscience-Public-v1.1). Apache License 2.0.
- aa_evals/gdpval/aa_prompts.py and quoted methodology passages in aa_evals/*/README.md  text quoted from Artificial
  Analysis' published methodology (https://artificialanalysis.ai/methodology), to reproduce their protocol.
- aa_evals/gdppdf/judge.py  judge prompt from the GDP.pdf harness (https://github.com/surge-ai/gdp-pdf), to
  reproduce its grading.
- m5/automationbench/ (synth-data)  uses schema code of AutomationBench (https://github.com/zapier/AutomationBench), MIT License,
